    {
      "text": "The baseline MnNiSi-based compound has a large magnetocaloric effect.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline MnNiSi-based compound is brittle and susceptible to fatigue cracking.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 3 at% Ag is an appropriate low-level addition to MnNiSi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Homogenization annealing near 900 °C will promote even Ag distribution and grain-boundary decoration in the modified MnNiSi alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ag atoms will segregate preferentially to grain boundaries and interfacial regions in MnNiSi.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ag segregation will reduce intergranular defects and produce a more uniform microstructure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ag will improve grain-boundary cohesion and reduce defect-induced crack initiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ag will act primarily as a structural modifier rather than a magnetic modifier.",
